Some Wizmode testing at Medusa showed that a pit dug with a pick-axe
adjacent to a water pool *mostly* (but not always) fills it with water.
Digging a hole, OTOH, (tested while flying above a sqare) always filled
the hole with water. It is not possible to dig a trench on solid land
and flood it by connecting it with the water.

BTW, Flying above a hole and making a watery connection from the pools
adjacent to the hole will not fill it, but flying above the hole and
zapping a wand of digging downwards will fill the _hole_ with water.
In my understanding a hole should not fill with water to create a pool.

